\newlabel{tab:calibration}{{4}{12}{Probability quality averaged across landmarks after fold and seed aggregation. Lower is better. ECE uses ten equal-width bins}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Probability quality and hypothetical decision utility. (A--C) Reliability diagrams use five equal-count probability-rank groups within each fitted model (35 patients per group); group coordinates are then averaged over folds and seeds. These groups describe calibration and differ from the ten fixed probability bins used for ECE. (D--F) Net-benefit curves under generic threshold-based positive actions, with treat-all and treat-none references. All curves use the original probabilities, without recalibration. No particular escalation or de-escalation decision is validated by this analysis.}}{12}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:calutility}{{4}{12}{Probability quality and hypothetical decision utility. (A--C) Reliability diagrams use five equal-count probability-rank groups within each fitted model (35 patients per group); group coordinates are then averaged over folds and seeds. These groups describe calibration and differ from the ten fixed probability bins used for ECE. (D--F) Net-benefit curves under generic threshold-based positive actions, with treat-all and treat-none references. All curves use the original probabilities, without recalibration. No particular escalation or de-escalation decision is validated by this analysis}{figure.4}{}}
